                <pb facs="0314" n="204" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg204"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.60p2/28: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Latvia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Coleman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-01-11T13:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 11,
                                1928—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 11—9:30
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>5. Paragraph 3 of Department’s telegram No. 19, May 16, 3 p.m., 1927, regarding
                    proposed United States-Latvian commercial treaty. In authorizing Legation to
                    accept Latvian proposal regarding article 27 did Department intend to approve
                    omission of last paragraph of article 26 of United States-Estonian treaty?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Coleman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
